{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #15 — e369 + parity epic 3e73. READ THIS, THEN #14, THEN #13. ===\n\nWORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family. ALWAYS: export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"\nCLOSES: run them from a worktree whose HEAD CONTAINS the commits — /Users/joeoakhart/agent-5200-diag\nis kept parked on origin/main for this. `--ref` does NOT satisfy the file_impact precheck (#13 trap 1).\nDO NOT trust the board below — read the tickets.\n\n*** SIX CHANGES MERGED. THE OPERATOR OVERRODE THE pip-audit BLOCK; ANOTHER SESSION FIXED THE CAUSE. ***\nMERGED: 1231 (5200 diagnosis+tests), 1232 (8d68 fix), 1233 (2944), 1234 (79d5), 1235 (cedc) — all on\nmain at bd3de0f864, content verified (three new test files present; `assignee_identity` in\ninbound_differ). Change 1239 (e47e, the click fix) was pushed with pip-audit GREEN on it and is\nowned by another session — DO NOT touch uv.lock or pyproject.toml.\nCLOSED: 2944 and 79d5. cedc's close was IN FLIGHT at writing.\nSTILL OPEN: e369 -> 5200, 8d68. 3e73 -> bd9e, cedc (P1) + 0fad, 2127 (P2, Cloud-side, MUST NOT gate).\n\n--- WHAT EACH REMAINING TICKET NEEDS ---\n * **8d68** — close FAILED on 2 criteria; BOTH are now handled or in flight:\n   1. \"cells 2 and 4 invert\". Cell 4 DID invert. **Cell 2 MUST NOT** — inverting it means asserting\n      the mint ACCEPTS a bare string, the one fix this ticket prohibits (on DC the scalar is `name`\n      and looks right; on Cloud it is the DISPLAY NAME and would register every Cloud user under the\n      wrong id). The implemented fix keeps the mint's dict guard and repairs the CALLER. I AMENDED\n      the criterion, recording that rationale in the description — the original wording prescribed a\n      mechanism that would have introduced the defect it was meant to prevent. Do not \"fix\" cell 2.\n   2. The J11 live cell needs a harness run. **30772461871 dispatched against main @ bd3de0f864**\n      (contains the fix). Read the per-cell verdict AND the\n      `[jira-live-canary] collected=N executed=N skipped=0` line, then record it on the ticket and\n      re-close. The pre-fix run 30767546938 failed that cell with \"THE PASS MINTED NOTHING\", so the\n      pair is a controlled before/after.\n * **5200** — same harness run settles it. Its last two cells were [04-transition-status] (already\n   green twice) and the assignee cell, which fails ONLY because of 8d68's product defect. Its oracle\n   is unchanged since 1226/1227, so a green cannot come from a weakened assertion.\n * **bd9e** — pushed as **1240 + 1241** (stacked, PS2), awaiting LLM-Review; CI re-running. Land,\n   then close. Its mutation verdict and diff proof are on the ticket.\n * **cedc** — merged as 1235; close in flight at writing.\n\n--- FOUR NEW TRAPS, ALL EXPENSIVE, ALL FOUND THIS STRETCH ---\n1. **A `Verified -1` CAN COME FROM A RUN THAT NEVER TESTED ANYTHING.** `gerrit-verify.yaml:40-43` sets\n   `concurrency: group: gerrit-verify-${{ inputs.GERRIT_CHANGE_ID || run_id }}` with\n   `cancel-in-progress: true`, and under multi-agent load it is NOT isolating per change as its\n   comment intends: dispatches 1-2s apart kill each other. The `vote` job is `if: always()`, so it\n   votes -1 off a CANCELLED run with `build-and-test` **SKIPPED** — zero tests executed.\n   CONSEQUENCES: rechecking two stacked changes in the same breath is self-defeating, and a recheck\n   can cancel ANOTHER agent's in-flight run. **SERIALIZE RECHECKS.** Diagnose a -1 by checking\n   whether build-and-test actually RAN (`gh run view <id> --repo navapbc/rebar --json jobs`), not by\n   reading logs.\n2. **`docs/env-vars.md` RECORDS LINE NUMBERS**, so a pure import-block insertion that shifts an\n   `os.environ.get` DOWN fails the env-var drift gate with zero env-var behaviour change. bd9e hit\n   this (`outbound_fields.py` :41 -> :49). Remedy: `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py`, folded into\n   the change that shifts the line — and note Gerrit verifies EACH change in a stack independently,\n   so regenerating once at a stack tip is not enough.\n3. **SHELL BACKTICKS IN A `rebar comment` ARGUMENT ARE COMMAND-SUBSTITUTED AND SILENTLY DELETE YOUR\n   TEXT.** I lost three load-bearing sentences on 8d68 that way — the ones naming what the fix does,\n   which is exactly what the close gate reads. The comment still landed at plausible length, so the\n   exit code and byte count both looked fine. **Write comment bodies to a file with a quoted\n   heredoc (`<<'EOF'`) and pass `\"$(cat file)\"`**, then grep the stored comment for the identifiers\n   you expect. This compounds the known `--body`/flock traps: verify CONTENT, not just length.\n4. **`constraint-dependencies` CANNOT LIFT AN UPSTREAM CAP — it only narrows.** I used it to \"prove\"\n   a click upgrade impossible and recorded that conclusion; a peer corrected me with\n   `override-dependencies`, which REPLACES the requirement and resolves cleanly to click 8.4.2. The\n   real capper is `inspect-ai` (`click!=8.2.0,<8.2.2,>=8.1.3`, unchanged through 0.3.251; upstream\n   PR UKGovernmentBEIS/inspect_ai#4596 open). I retracted the wrong half on e47e. Lesson: when a\n   resolver says UNSATISFIABLE, check whether your TOOL could ever have said otherwise.\n\n--- ALSO FILED ---\n * **9fb3-ab66-2a81-4940** — a real inspect-ai eval smoke test. The `[eval]` path has NO CI coverage\n   and, because `[tool.uv] conflicts` declares `eval` and `dev` mutually conflicting, it structurally\n   CANNOT get any from the normal suite; it needs its own lane. Gap predates the click change.\n * **a3fa-e8d4-f4aa-4b51** — the four capability call sites are `cast(...)` but not runtime-guarded,\n   unlike `fetcher.py:553/590` which gate on `hasattr`. Safe today only via upstream capability\n   gating that nothing local asserts, and the failure would be SILENT (AttributeError inside a broad\n   `except Exception`).\n * **049e-9fac-a821-4ea2** — DC's comment ceiling is admin-configurable and rebar hardcodes the\n   default. Neither this nor a3fa is an e369 child; reasoning is recorded on each, and reparenting is\n   one command if the operator prefers the stricter reading.\n\n--- THE EVIDENCE THAT VINDICATES THE WHOLE PARITY THESIS (worth keeping) ---\n * 2944's ledger ran the 429 mutation under the ORIGINAL assertions and it **passed green** — a\n   direct demonstration that the old test could not fail, not an argument that it couldn't.\n * cedc's `WIKI_DESCRIPTION_LIMIT 32767 -> 32766` mutation initially SURVIVED because its at-limit\n   pins derived their boundary from the IMPORTED constant. 79d5's agent independently hit the same\n   defect class in different files. Both fixed by pinning a module-local literal.\n * 79d5: dropping the DC sanitizer injection left CONVERGENCE passing, because DC's and Cloud's\n   comment truncation output is byte-identical — only the recording check caught it.\n * 8d68 exists at all because the assignee oracle was vacuous; repaired, it immediately found a real\n   DC defect that had been reported green for months."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785714516886080001,"uuid":"2acd8044-c900-4772-b7f7-121c19e0b976"}